      "sourceFeatureExtractionItemID": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "As someone who uses a Custom Instance ID for their weekly event I found it extremely disappointing that the \"Close Instance\" button not only prevented new people from joining for that event like I wanted, but it prevented people from joining any future event.\n\nEven a month later using the Instance Link and clicking \"Invite Me\" does nothing. Why? Why can't the ID be recycled after like 24hrs, a week, or even a month. Why is it just dead for the rest of time.\n\nI had to go through every location where I advertised our weekly event and change the link to be every so slightly different so it worked again, and I for sure am not going to do that every week if I were to keep using the \"Close Instance\" feature. \n\nThis issue has made the feature completely useless for me. I hope this gets changed soon, because it would make the feature EXTREMELY useful when it does.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
